infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Conformist vs Anticorruption Layer
  desc Same upstream you cannot change — opposite translation strategy and blast radius
  compares
    - label Conformist: adopt the upstream model
      children
        - label No translation layer
          desc Use the supplier's types directly inside your domain model
        - label Upstream language wins
          desc Its terms enter your ubiquitous language; you lose model autonomy
        - label Cheap upfront
          desc No translation code to write, maintain, or test
        - label Migration blast radius: everywhere
          desc An upstream change touches signatures, events, DB columns, and fixtures across the codebase
    - label Anticorruption Layer: translate at the boundary
      children
        - label Explicit translation layer
          desc Speaks the supplier's language outside, your language inside
        - label Your language wins
          desc Model stays yours; it evolves with your domain experts, not their API
        - label Costly upfront
          desc Translation code to write, maintain, and test
        - label Migration blast radius: one component
          desc An upstream change is contained — you rewrite only the ACL
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
